      "section": "Microwave power test: measuring the microwave power output of the magnetron(s)",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 39.12,
        "t": 787.00791953125,
        "r": 509.28,
        "b": 776.2243393785782
      },
      "content": "Microwave power test: measuring the microwave power output of the magnetron(s)",
      "level": 2,
      "role": "section"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0650",
      "reading_order": 833,
      "section": "Microwave power test: measuring the microwave power output of the magnetron(s)",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 36.0,
        "t": 759.5459195312501,
        "r": 265.743,
        "b": 751.4582344167462
      },
      "content": "Check that the following requirements have been met:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0651",
      "reading_order": 834,
      "section": "Microwave power test: measuring the microwave power output of the magnetron(s)",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 54.00000000000003,
        "t": 747.54891953125,
        "r": 447.29999999999995,
        "b": 739.0982344167462
      },
      "content": " The appliance is cool. This test will not operate at a cavity temperature of 100 o C or above."
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig_0135",
      "reading_order": 835,
      "section": "Microwave power test: measuring the microwave power output of the magnetron(s)",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 24.81888704114895,
        "t": 726.8382652133023,
        "r": 236.77402234444506,
        "b": 597.1562775468292
      },
      "image_path": "figures/figure_0135.png",
      "previous_block_id": "txt_0651",
      "next_block_id": "txt_0652",
      "image_hash": "76c36a2ed2f6ba1304f1747199152142ca18bfdefd3417b4f76f0938c2995310",
      "width": 212,
      "height": 129
    },
    {
      "type": "admonition",
      "id": "txt_0652",
      "reading_order": 836,
      "severity": "note",
      "content": "NOTE: The power output is established under IEC 705 standard method which is only workable in laboratory-controlled conditions. The power output is also affected by line voltage under load, so this test is an approximation only.",
      "section": "NOTE:",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 36.0,
        "t": 582.5460195312501,
        "r": 65.7,
        "b": 574.3587304760582
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0654",
      "reading_order": 838,
      "section": "NOTE:",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 53.98200000000012,
        "t": 533.4690195312502,
        "r": 283.9680000000001,
        "b": 525.2817304760583
      },
      "content": "Ensure the cavity is close to ambient temperature."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0655",
      "reading_order": 839,
      "section": "NOTE:",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 53.9910000000001,
        "t": 521.2290195312502,
        "r": 212.45400000000006,
        "b": 513.0417304760583
      },
      "content": "Enter the Service Settings / Tests."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0656",
      "reading_order": 840,
      "section": "NOTE:",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 53.99100000000004,
        "t": 508.9890195312501,
        "r": 542.4390000000001,
        "b": 500.80173047605837
      },
      "content": "Fill a microwave safe container (glass or plastic) with one litre (1.78 pints) of cool tap water, ideally at 20°C (68°F)."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0657",
      "reading_order": 841,
      "section": "NOTE:",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 53.982000000000085,
        "t": 496.9920195312501,
        "r": 526.623,
        "b": 476.6583344167462
      },
      "content": "Measure and record the water temperature in the container using a thermometer capable of reading ±0.1 o C increments."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0658",
      "reading_order": 842,
      "section": "NOTE:",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 54.00600000000003,
        "t": 472.26301953125,
        "r": 255.63299999999998,
        "b": 464.07573047605825
      },
      "content": "Place the container centrally into the cavity."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0659",
      "reading_order": 843,
      "section": "NOTE:",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 53.97,
        "t": 460.26601953125,
        "r": 551.787,
        "b": 439.82133441674614
      },
      "content": "Select 'Microwave Power' from the service settings tests (microwave power 100% for 60 seconds, convection fan at 10%)."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0660",
      "reading_order": 844,
      "section": "NOTE:",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 54.0,
        "t": 292.50601953125,
        "r": 555.057,
        "b": 272.06133441674615
      },
      "content": "When the countdown has finished, remove the container from the cavity. Immediately stir with a plastic implement and measure the water temperature."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0661",
      "reading_order": 845,
      "section": "NOTE:",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 54.00899999999999,
        "t": 255.55201953124993,
        "r": 457.27199999999993,
        "b": 247.46433441674617
      },
      "content": "Calculate the temperature rise of the water (end temperature minus the start temperature)."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0662",
      "reading_order": 846,
      "section": "NOTE:",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 54.00899999999996,
        "t": 243.42901953125,
        "r": 452.34000000000003,
        "b": 234.9813344167461
      },
      "content": " The temperature rise should be 14.3°C (25.7°F) ±10% for the 1000W (1 magnetron) variant."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0663",
      "reading_order": 847,
      "section": "NOTE:",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 54.00000000000006,
        "t": 231.18901953124998,
        "r": 456.5340000000001,
        "b": 222.7413344167461
      },
      "content": " The temperature rise should be 28.5°C (51.4°F) ±10% for the 2000W (2 magnetrons) variant."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0664",
      "reading_order": 848,
      "section": "NOTE:",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 53.991000000000156,
        "t": 219.19201953125003,
        "r": 559.7460000000002,
        "b": 186.26433441674612
      },
      "content": " If the temperature rise is outside these limits repeat test and/or check the microwave circuit and components. A low reading could be caused by the water container absorbing the energy, in which case an alternative container should be used."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0665",
      "reading_order": 849,
      "section": "NOTE:",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 54.0,
        "t": 182.34601953125002,
        "r": 450.40500000000003,
        "b": 173.89833441674614
      },
      "content": " Replace the faulty HV component if required (see High voltage components in section 5.8)."
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig_0136",
      "reading_order": 850,
      "section": "NOTE:",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 54.0634792017997,
        "t": 425.4102027894021,
        "r": 461.959010175578,
        "b": 306.68660992320326
      },
      "image_path": "figures/figure_0136.png",
      "previous_block_id": "txt_0665",
      "next_block_id": "txt_0666",
      "image_hash": "7b735f64aab7285fa50063071d5196c307b80da3c1d2192787ea3cd1a8e070be",
      "width": 408,
      "height": 119
    },
    {
      "type": "admonition",
      "id": "txt_0666",
      "reading_order": 851,
      "section": "NOTE:",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 50.4,
        "t": 157.50601953125,
        "r": 417.16799999999995,
        "b": 149.31873047605825
      },
      "content": "Note: Opening the door during the test will stop the test. Reselect the test to run again.",
      "severity": "note"
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0667",
      "reading_order": 852,
      "section": "NOTE:",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 54.0,
        "t": 133.02601953124997,
        "r": 368.45099999999996,
        "b": 124.93833441674622
      },
      "content": "On completion of the test, specify the result by selecting 'Pass' or 'Fail'."
    },
